# Database Schema

Reference: `supabase/migrations/20250222000000_initial_schema.sql`

## Tables

| Table | Key Columns | Notes |
|-------|-------------|-------|
| **resumes** | `id`, `user_id`, `parsed_data` (JSONB) | No file storage; `parsed_data` matches `ResumeData` |
| **analyses** | `id`, `user_id`, `resume_id`, `job_snapshot` (JSONB), `score`, `matched_skills`, `missing_technical_skills`, `missing_behavioral_skills`, `status` | Job stored as snapshot; `status`: pending \| completed \| abandoned |
| **user_credits** | `user_id`, `credits`, `updated_at` | One row per user; created when user uploads or creates a resume (3 credits); decremented on successful analysis |
| **optimized_documents** | `id`, `analysis_id`, `file_path`, `format` ('pdf'\|'docx') | Access via analysis ownership |

## Column Mapping

- **resumes.parsed_data** — Validated with `resumeDataSchema` from `@/schemas/resume`
- **analyses.job_snapshot** — `{ title, company, rawText }`; validated with `jobSnapshotSchema` from `@/schemas/job`
- **analyses.matched_skills** — `string[]` in JSONB
- **analyses.missing_technical_skills**, **missing_behavioral_skills** — `string[]` in JSONB; set from gap analysis AI result; used by synthesis and chat
- **analyses.status** — `'pending' | 'completed' | 'abandoned'`; set in `runGapAnalysis` (pending) and `synthesizeOptimizedResumeForPreview` (completed)

## RLS

- resumes, analyses, user_credits: users access only their own rows (`auth.uid() = user_id`)
- optimized_documents: SELECT/INSERT via analysis ownership
        